  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The current world search system only appears to use the user-created descriptions and title as search terms, which does not work between different languages, or when someone has cryptically titled/described their world.\n\nTo help improve the quality of these results, I suggest:\n\nA community tagging system. Allow Known/Trusted world visitors to select/vote from a list of pre-determined keywords which convey the mood, purpose, and aesthetic of a given world. \n\nThese would include categories of terms that could be amended over time;\n\nLocation/aesthetic - Church, Beach, Sky, City, Lake, etc\n\nMood - Somber, Upbeat, Chill, Relaxed, Quiet, Lonely, etc\n\nPurpose - Game, Sleep, Idle, Social, Market, Avatars, etc.\n\nThis could improve search, and add the option to filter by world type!",
